1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,430
One hundred and fifty dollars.

2
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:05,750
That's what thousands of Australians
paid in November 2019 to reserve a spot

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,170
in the queue for the most talked-about
vehicle on the planet the Tesla

4
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,370
Cybertruck.

5
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:12,050
They waited through a pandemic.

6
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:15,970
They waited while the reservation
page quietly disappeared in 2022.

7
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:20,790
They watched Tesla parade a Cybertruck
around Australian showrooms in 2024.

8
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:24,230
They heard Tesla's local boss say he
was personally confident it would come.

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:30,270
Then, on Friday the 23rd of October
2026 almost seven years after they paid

10
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:31,770
the email arrived.

11
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:34,030
Quote: "After careful consideration,

12
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,870
plans to produce Cybertruck for
Australia and New Zealand have been

13
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,750
discontinued." That's it.

14
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:39,770
No Cybertruck.

15
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:40,650
Not now.

16
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:43,030
Not ever, according to Tesla's own plans.

17
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:44,410
So what actually happened?

18
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:46,530
Why did Tesla walk away from Australia?

19
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,290
What does the refund look like?

20
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,830
And with the Cybertruck gone,

21
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:54,390
which electric and American utes
can Aussies actually buy in 2026?

22
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,070
Stay with me,

23
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:58,330
because the real reason the Cybertruck
died says a lot about where the whole

24
00:00:58,380 --> 00:00:59,520
ute market is heading.

25
00:01:00,108 --> 00:01:03,438
To understand why this hurts,
you have to go back to the start.

26
00:01:03,488 --> 00:01:05,218
In November 2019,

27
00:01:05,268 --> 00:01:09,178
Elon Musk walked on stage in Los
Angeles and revealed the Cybertruck.

28
00:01:09,228 --> 00:01:10,148
Stainless steel body.

29
00:01:10,198 --> 00:01:14,318
Armoured glass which famously cracked
on stage when a metal ball was thrown at

30
00:01:14,368 --> 00:01:14,778
it.

31
00:01:14,828 --> 00:01:19,998
And a promised starting price in
the United States of just $39,900,

32
00:01:20,048 --> 00:01:24,168
with the top tri-motor version
promising more than 500 miles around 800

33
00:01:24,218 --> 00:01:25,458
kilometres of range.

34
00:01:25,508 --> 00:01:27,658
The internet went wild.

35
00:01:27,708 --> 00:01:29,818
Reservations opened almost immediately,

36
00:01:29,868 --> 00:01:34,118
including in Australia, with
a $150 refundable deposit.

37
00:01:34,168 --> 00:01:39,058
Tesla has said tens of thousands of
people reserved between 2019 and 2021.

38
00:01:39,108 --> 00:01:41,158
For Aussies, the idea made sense.

39
00:01:41,208 --> 00:01:42,058
We love utes.

40
00:01:42,108 --> 00:01:43,018
We love towing.

41
00:01:43,068 --> 00:01:46,578
And here was an electric pickup that
promised to do it all with a futuristic

42
00:01:46,628 --> 00:01:49,138
look nothing else on the road could match.

43
00:01:49,188 --> 00:01:50,918
But there was a problem from day one.

44
00:01:50,968 --> 00:01:53,978
The Cybertruck was designed as a
left-hand-drive American truck.

45
00:01:54,028 --> 00:01:56,058
Australia drives on the left,

46
00:01:56,108 --> 00:01:58,558
and our cars need the
steering wheel on the right.

47
00:01:58,608 --> 00:02:01,238
Converting a vehicle like
this isn't a quick job.

48
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:03,138
It means re-engineering the dashboard,

49
00:02:03,188 --> 00:02:05,998
the steering, the pedals,
and testing it all again.

50
00:02:06,048 --> 00:02:10,538
And when the Cybertruck finally reached
American customers at the end of 2023

51
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:14,398
four years after the reveal it was
more expensive and had less range than

52
00:02:14,448 --> 00:02:15,838
originally promised.

53
00:02:15,888 --> 00:02:19,008
The dream and the reality had
already started to drift apart.

54
00:02:19,868 --> 00:02:23,398
For a few years, Australian
reservation holders lived on hope.

55
00:02:23,448 --> 00:02:27,458
In May 2022, Tesla closed
the local reservation page.

56
00:02:27,508 --> 00:02:29,478
It didn't refund deposits automatically.

57
00:02:29,528 --> 00:02:32,278
It just replaced the page
with a "get updates" button.

58
00:02:32,328 --> 00:02:35,278
Most people simply
forgot about their $150.

59
00:02:35,328 --> 00:02:38,998
Then, in 2024, the hope came roaring back.

60
00:02:39,048 --> 00:02:42,918
Tesla Australia imported a Cybertruck
and took it on a national roadshow,

61
00:02:42,968 --> 00:02:45,518
showing it at events and
showrooms around the country.

62
00:02:45,568 --> 00:02:47,218
People queued to take photos.

63
00:02:47,268 --> 00:02:48,558
That same year,

64
00:02:48,608 --> 00:02:52,078
Musk told shareholders they might be
able to certify the Cybertruck for other

65
00:02:52,128 --> 00:02:54,198
markets "sometime next year".

66
00:02:54,248 --> 00:02:55,398
In March 2025,

67
00:02:55,448 --> 00:02:58,188
Tesla's Australia and New
Zealand country director,

68
00:02:58,238 --> 00:03:02,118
Thom Drew, said he was "personally
confident" the Cybertruck would come

69
00:03:02,168 --> 00:03:04,418
possibly as early as 2026.

70
00:03:04,468 --> 00:03:06,758
Within about a month,
his tone had changed.

71
00:03:06,808 --> 00:03:08,818
He said he was "not confident it's coming,

72
00:03:08,868 --> 00:03:11,658
but we are discussing it." By May 2025,

73
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:14,778
the local team had been briefed on the
Australian Design Rule changes that

74
00:03:14,828 --> 00:03:17,078
would be needed including bumper widths,

75
00:03:17,128 --> 00:03:19,438
external lighting, and of
course right-hand drive.

76
00:03:19,488 --> 00:03:21,178
And then came the silence.

77
00:03:21,228 --> 00:03:23,028
Until October 2026.

78
00:03:23,909 --> 00:03:26,079
So why did Tesla finally pull the plug?

79
00:03:26,129 --> 00:03:29,659
Tesla hasn't given a detailed
public reason beyond that email.

80
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:32,199
But the numbers tell
the story very clearly.

81
00:03:32,249 --> 00:03:33,159
Start with sales.

82
00:03:33,209 --> 00:03:37,759
Musk once predicted the Cybertruck
could sell 250,000 a year.

83
00:03:37,809 --> 00:03:39,799
The reality has been very different.

84
00:03:39,849 --> 00:03:46,759
According to estimates reported by
CarExpert, around 38,965 were sold in 2024.

85
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:51,219
That fell to about 20,237 in 2025.

86
00:03:51,269 --> 00:03:53,379
And from January to September 2026,

87
00:03:53,429 --> 00:03:58,259
it was around 11,586 down
another twenty-eight per cent.

88
00:03:58,309 --> 00:03:59,819
Then there's the price.

89
00:03:59,869 --> 00:04:04,859
The truck that was supposed to start
at $39,900 now sells for around eighty

90
00:04:04,909 --> 00:04:08,219
thousand US dollars for the
dual-motor version in America.

91
00:04:08,269 --> 00:04:10,539
EV Central estimated that in Australia,

92
00:04:10,589 --> 00:04:15,039
it would likely have cost around
$130,000 before on-road costs and local

93
00:04:15,089 --> 00:04:15,779
taxes.

94
00:04:15,829 --> 00:04:17,419
That's a very hard sell.

95
00:04:17,469 --> 00:04:18,839
Then there's right-hand drive.

96
00:04:18,889 --> 00:04:21,179
The Cybertruck is built
only in left-hand drive.

97
00:04:21,229 --> 00:04:23,779
It isn't sold in any
right-hand-drive market.

98
00:04:23,829 --> 00:04:27,559
Australia would likely have been the
main one other right-hand-drive markets

99
00:04:27,609 --> 00:04:31,559
like the UK and Japan aren't natural
homes for a truck this big either.

100
00:04:31,609 --> 00:04:35,019
Building a right-hand-drive version just
for us would mean spending a fortune

101
00:04:35,069 --> 00:04:36,652
for a tiny number of sales.

102
00:04:36,702 --> 00:04:39,199
And finally, the size of the market.

103
00:04:39,249 --> 00:04:43,639
The whole full-size American pickup
segment in Australia trucks like the Ram,

104
00:04:43,689 --> 00:04:47,999
the Chevrolet Silverado and the Ford
F-150 sells roughly ten thousand vehicles

105
00:04:48,049 --> 00:04:48,939
a year.

106
00:04:48,989 --> 00:04:50,859
Even if Tesla grabbed a big slice of that,

107
00:04:50,909 --> 00:04:54,359
it would never justify the cost of
re-engineering and certifying the

108
00:04:54,409 --> 00:04:56,119
Cybertruck for local roads.

109
00:04:56,169 --> 00:04:59,379
Put all of that together, and the
decision was almost made for them.

110
00:04:59,429 --> 00:05:03,319
And there's one more factor: the
Cybertruck's track record in America.

111
00:05:03,369 --> 00:05:05,389
According to the official
US recall database,

112
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:09,299
the Cybertruck has been recalled
eleven times since it launched.

113
00:05:09,349 --> 00:05:10,939
In April 2024,

114
00:05:10,989 --> 00:05:14,379
it was recalled because the accelerator
pedal pad could come loose and get

115
00:05:14,429 --> 00:05:17,799
trapped by the interior trim which could
cause the truck to keep accelerating.

116
00:05:17,849 --> 00:05:19,329
In March 2025,

117
00:05:19,379 --> 00:05:23,959
more than 46,000 trucks were recalled
because an exterior trim panel could

118
00:05:24,009 --> 00:05:25,539
detach while driving.

119
00:05:25,589 --> 00:05:27,379
In October 2025,

120
00:05:27,429 --> 00:05:30,919
more than 63,000 were recalled because
the front parking lights were too

121
00:05:30,969 --> 00:05:32,899
bright to meet US rules.

122
00:05:32,949 --> 00:05:34,739
And in April 2026,

123
00:05:34,789 --> 00:05:37,959
there was a recall over brake
rotor stud holes that could crack,

124
00:05:38,009 --> 00:05:39,809
allowing a wheel stud to separate.

125
00:05:39,859 --> 00:05:44,019
Recalls happen to every brand, and
a recall is the system working.

126
00:05:44,069 --> 00:05:47,479
But for a low-volume truck that would
have needed expensive local engineering,

127
00:05:47,529 --> 00:05:51,489
every extra problem made the
Australian business case even weaker.

128
00:05:52,294 --> 00:05:55,034
So what do Aussie reservation
holders actually get?

129
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:59,384
Tesla says reservations will be
cancelled and deposits refunded in full.

130
00:05:59,434 --> 00:06:02,664
Customers will get a separate email
to confirm their refund details,

131
00:06:02,714 --> 00:06:06,624
and EV Central reports the money
should arrive within thirty days.

132
00:06:06,674 --> 00:06:08,604
And Tesla has added a sweetener.

133
00:06:08,654 --> 00:06:13,344
Reservation holders who order a new
Model 3 or Model Y get one year of Full

134
00:06:13,394 --> 00:06:15,444
Self-Driving Supervised for free.

135
00:06:15,494 --> 00:06:21,664
At the current price of $149
a month, that's worth $1,788.

136
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:24,504
Now, it's worth being
clear about what that is.

137
00:06:24,554 --> 00:06:26,524
"Supervised" means exactly that.

138
00:06:26,574 --> 00:06:28,244
The driver must stay alert,

139
00:06:28,294 --> 00:06:32,484
keep their hands ready and remain fully
responsible for the car at all times.

140
00:06:32,534 --> 00:06:35,804
It's a driver assistance feature,
not a car that drives itself.

141
00:06:35,854 --> 00:06:39,744
If you paid a deposit back in 2019
and you've changed your email address,

142
00:06:39,794 --> 00:06:42,904
or you can't find the message,
contact Tesla directly.

143
00:06:42,954 --> 00:06:45,964
A $150 refund isn't life-changing,

144
00:06:46,014 --> 00:06:49,374
but it's your money, and after
seven years you're entitled to it.

145
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,900
Quick favour before we keep going.

146
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:55,220
Did you put down a deposit
for a Cybertruck back in 2019?

147
00:06:55,270 --> 00:06:56,820
Or did you see it on the roadshow?

148
00:06:56,870 --> 00:07:00,340
Tell me in the comments I want to know
how many of you were in that queue.

149
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:01,310
And if you want honest,

150
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:05,080
fact-checked videos about the
Aussie car market in 2026,

151
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,110
hit subscribe and turn on notifications.

152
00:07:08,103 --> 00:07:09,613
Here's the interesting part.

153
00:07:09,663 --> 00:07:11,753
Tesla isn't struggling in Australia.

154
00:07:11,803 --> 00:07:13,813
It's the Cybertruck that didn't fit.

155
00:07:13,863 --> 00:07:15,833
In September 2026,

156
00:07:15,883 --> 00:07:19,493
Tesla sold 5,654 cars in Australia,

157
00:07:19,543 --> 00:07:22,793
up more than twenty-one per cent
on the same month last year.

158
00:07:22,843 --> 00:07:27,653
Electric vehicles made up 24.2 per cent
of all new car sales that month more

159
00:07:27,703 --> 00:07:30,293
than petrol cars, for the
second month in a row.

160
00:07:30,343 --> 00:07:33,853
And with a fuel crisis pushing diesel
towards three dollars a litre in some

161
00:07:33,903 --> 00:07:38,013
capital cities, more Aussies than ever
are thinking about going electric.

162
00:07:38,063 --> 00:07:40,373
You can see it in the insurance data too.

163
00:07:40,423 --> 00:07:44,283
NRMA Insurance says requests for
electric vehicle insurance quotes were up

164
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:47,653
eighty per cent in the
first nine months of 2026.

165
00:07:47,703 --> 00:07:51,613
And NRMA's own survey found the share
of Australians actively considering a

166
00:07:51,663 --> 00:07:56,633
battery electric car rose from twenty
per cent in 2024 to thirty-one per cent

167
00:07:56,683 --> 00:07:58,353
in 2026.

168
00:07:58,403 --> 00:08:01,313
The demand for electric
vehicles in Australia is real.

169
00:08:01,363 --> 00:08:05,433
It just isn't demand for a
$130,000 stainless steel truck.

170
00:08:05,483 --> 00:08:09,273
In fact, 2026 has been a
record year for Tesla here.

171
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:14,753
In June, Tesla sold 8,670 vehicles in
Australia the strongest month in its

172
00:08:14,803 --> 00:08:18,053
local history, according to
Electric Vehicle Council figures.

173
00:08:18,103 --> 00:08:21,533
The Model Y alone sold 8,072 that month,

174
00:08:21,583 --> 00:08:26,993
and 20,396 in the first half of the
year up more than ninety-five per cent.

175
00:08:27,043 --> 00:08:32,533
Tesla's first-half total was 23,588,
up almost sixty-seven per cent.

176
00:08:32,583 --> 00:08:36,333
A big part of that came from
the new six-seat Model Y L.

177
00:08:36,383 --> 00:08:37,813
It's not all good news.

178
00:08:37,863 --> 00:08:41,573
The Model 3 has gone backwards,
down forty-seven per cent in June.

179
00:08:41,623 --> 00:08:44,753
And BYD's Sealion 7 has
become a serious rival,

180
00:08:44,803 --> 00:08:48,573
with 7,786 deliveries through May.

181
00:08:48,623 --> 00:08:52,213
But overall, Tesla is having one of
its best years ever in Australia.

182
00:08:52,263 --> 00:08:54,213
So Tesla's message is clear.

183
00:08:54,263 --> 00:08:58,233
It would rather put its effort into the
Model Y and Model 3 cars that already

184
00:08:58,283 --> 00:09:00,753
sell in big numbers
here than into a niche,

185
00:09:00,803 --> 00:09:03,613
left-hand-drive truck that
would cost a fortune to convert.

186
00:09:03,663 --> 00:09:05,073
That's a business decision.

187
00:09:05,123 --> 00:09:08,633
But for the people who waited seven
years, it's still a disappointment.

188
00:09:08,683 --> 00:09:12,363
And it raises a bigger question:
if not the Cybertruck, then what?

189
00:09:13,212 --> 00:09:15,342
Let's look at the big
American pickups first,

190
00:09:15,392 --> 00:09:18,342
because that's the segment the
Cybertruck would have competed in.

191
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:21,002
Australia already has the Ram 1500,

192
00:09:21,052 --> 00:09:24,002
the Chevrolet Silverado
and the Ford F-150,

193
00:09:24,052 --> 00:09:26,642
all converted to right-hand
drive for our market.

194
00:09:26,692 --> 00:09:30,682
In March 2026, the F-150 sold 270,

195
00:09:30,732 --> 00:09:36,322
the Ram 1500 sold 181,
and the Silverado 172.

196
00:09:36,372 --> 00:09:39,902
These are big, expensive trucks,
and they sell in small numbers.

197
00:09:39,952 --> 00:09:41,462
And they've had their
own problems this year.

198
00:09:41,512 --> 00:09:47,412
In October 2026, Ford recalled the
F-150 in Australia over a fire risk.

199
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:51,742
CarExpert notes Ford issues more
recalls here than any other car maker.

200
00:09:51,792 --> 00:09:54,182
And there's a reason these
trucks cost so much here.

201
00:09:54,232 --> 00:09:56,862
They aren't built in right-hand
drive at the factory.

202
00:09:56,912 --> 00:10:01,302
The Ram 1500 and the Chevrolet Silverado
are remanufactured in Melbourne by

203
00:10:01,352 --> 00:10:03,102
the Walkinshaw Automotive Group,

204
00:10:03,152 --> 00:10:07,442
and the F-150 is converted by RMA
Automotive, also in Melbourne.

205
00:10:07,492 --> 00:10:11,262
Each truck arrives in left-hand drive
and is partly taken apart and rebuilt

206
00:10:11,312 --> 00:10:13,062
with the steering on the right.

207
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:16,842
It's skilled, expensive work and it's
a big part of why these pickups cost

208
00:10:16,892 --> 00:10:19,722
more than a hundred thousand
dollars in many versions.

209
00:10:19,772 --> 00:10:22,422
That's exactly the work the
Cybertruck would have needed.

210
00:10:22,472 --> 00:10:25,082
Except with its unusual
steer-by-wire system,

211
00:10:25,132 --> 00:10:28,102
its giant central screen and
its stainless steel body,

212
00:10:28,152 --> 00:10:31,842
it would have been even more complicated
unless Tesla built a right-hand-drive

213
00:10:31,892 --> 00:10:32,982
version itself.

214
00:10:33,032 --> 00:10:34,562
The lesson is simple.

215
00:10:34,612 --> 00:10:37,942
Even the established American
trucks are a niche in Australia.

216
00:10:37,992 --> 00:10:40,342
The Cybertruck would have
been a niche within a niche.

217
00:10:40,392 --> 00:10:43,922
And Tesla isn't the only company that
has quietly walked away from a promise

218
00:10:43,972 --> 00:10:45,212
in 2026.

219
00:10:45,262 --> 00:10:49,882
Isuzu has cancelled its plans to
bring the electric D-Max to Australia.

220
00:10:49,932 --> 00:10:53,042
Nissan has indefinitely postponed
the new-generation Leaf here,

221
00:10:53,092 --> 00:10:56,202
and cut the Juke and the
Pathfinder from its range.

222
00:10:56,252 --> 00:10:59,962
Jaguar stopped selling new petrol cars
in Australia on the 31st of December

223
00:11:00,012 --> 00:11:05,262
2025, and still has no confirmed local
launch date for its new electric models

224
00:11:05,312 --> 00:11:08,362
which means it sold zero
new cars here in September.

225
00:11:08,412 --> 00:11:12,822
And Volvo has axed the S60 sedan and
the V60 Cross Country wagon from its

226
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:14,002
local line-up.

227
00:11:14,052 --> 00:11:18,262
In a market this crowded with around
seventy brands fighting for roughly 1.2

228
00:11:18,312 --> 00:11:21,802
million sales a year car
makers are being ruthless.

229
00:11:21,852 --> 00:11:23,982
If a model can't sell
in big enough numbers,

230
00:11:24,032 --> 00:11:26,072
it doesn't come, or it doesn't stay.

231
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:30,160
Now let's talk about the vehicle Australians
were really hoping the Cybertruck

232
00:11:30,210 --> 00:11:32,420
would be: an electric ute.

233
00:11:32,470 --> 00:11:34,320
Here's the reality in 2026.

234
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:38,860
Electric utes make up less than one
per cent of Australian ute sales.

235
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:40,320
According to CarExpert,

236
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:44,880
there were 157,531 ute
deliveries to September,

237
00:11:44,930 --> 00:11:48,200
and diesel and plug-in
hybrids still dominate.

238
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:50,260
Toyota launched the HiLux BEV,

239
00:11:50,310 --> 00:11:52,740
the electric version of the
country's most famous ute.

240
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:56,380
But it sold roughly 300
between May and early July,

241
00:11:56,430 --> 00:11:58,980
with fewer than ten
going to private buyers.

242
00:11:59,030 --> 00:12:03,600
KGM's Musso EV has sold just over
300 since its launch late last year.

243
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:07,140
And Isuzu has cancelled its plans
to bring the D-Max EV to Australia

244
00:12:07,190 --> 00:12:08,240
altogether.

245
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:10,260
As Isuzu's Rod Caldwell put it:

246
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:13,100
"Customers don't want
it." Not everyone agrees.

247
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:17,140
In September 2026, MG confirmed the U9 EV,

248
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:23,620
an all-electric dual-cab ute, priced
from $78,990 before on-road costs.

249
00:12:23,670 --> 00:12:26,600
It claims 430 kilometres of range,

250
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:29,060
325 kilowatts of power,

251
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:34,220
and crucially for Aussie buyers
3,500 kilograms of braked towing.

252
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:37,860
It can charge from twenty to eighty per
cent in about forty-two minutes on a

253
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:42,340
fast charger, and carry a
payload of 685 kilograms.

254
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:45,490
Deliveries start in the
last quarter of 2026.

255
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:48,720
MG says customers here have been
"yearning" for a vehicle like this.

256
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:51,420
And then there's the plug-in
hybrid middle ground,

257
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:53,380
led by the BYD Shark 6,

258
00:12:53,430 --> 00:12:57,340
which was the third best-selling 4x4
pick-up in Australia across the first

259
00:12:57,390 --> 00:13:02,160
half of 2026 a remarkable result for a
ute that only arrived at the start of

260
00:13:02,210 --> 00:13:02,930
2025.

261
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:06,920
GAC has confirmed its upcoming
ute will be electrified only,

262
00:13:06,970 --> 00:13:10,840
and Chery's Stockman plug-in
hybrid is due late in 2026.

263
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:12,340
So the electric ute is coming.

264
00:13:12,390 --> 00:13:15,230
It just doesn't look like a
stainless steel spaceship.

265
00:13:16,124 --> 00:13:17,814
So what does all this mean for you?

266
00:13:17,864 --> 00:13:19,574
If you had a Cybertruck reservation,

267
00:13:19,624 --> 00:13:22,854
check your email including your
spam folder for Tesla's message,

268
00:13:22,904 --> 00:13:24,814
and follow the refund process.

269
00:13:24,864 --> 00:13:26,974
If you've moved or changed email address,

270
00:13:27,024 --> 00:13:30,854
contact Tesla directly with
any details you have from 2019.

271
00:13:30,904 --> 00:13:33,134
If you're thinking about
a big American pickup,

272
00:13:33,184 --> 00:13:34,494
remember they're expensive,

273
00:13:34,544 --> 00:13:37,714
thirsty and sold in small
numbers so check recalls,

274
00:13:37,764 --> 00:13:40,754
service locations and resale
values before you buy.

275
00:13:40,804 --> 00:13:43,754
If you want an electric ute, think
hard about how you'll use it.

276
00:13:43,804 --> 00:13:46,294
Range drops when you tow heavy loads.

277
00:13:46,344 --> 00:13:48,074
If you do long trips with a caravan,

278
00:13:48,124 --> 00:13:50,574
a plug-in hybrid may
suit you better for now.

279
00:13:50,624 --> 00:13:53,074
If you mostly do short
runs and charge at home,

280
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:56,914
a fully electric ute could save you a
lot on fuel especially with fuel prices

281
00:13:56,964 --> 00:13:58,874
where they are in 2026.

282
00:13:58,924 --> 00:14:00,974
And there's a bigger
lesson about deposits.

283
00:14:01,024 --> 00:14:02,954
A reservation is not a promise.

284
00:14:03,004 --> 00:14:05,774
Before you put money down for
a car that doesn't exist yet,

285
00:14:05,824 --> 00:14:07,874
ask whether the deposit
is fully refundable,

286
00:14:07,924 --> 00:14:09,034
how you'll get it back,

287
00:14:09,084 --> 00:14:12,034
and whether there's any date by
which the company has to deliver.

288
00:14:12,084 --> 00:14:15,514
Seven years is a long time to
wait for a car that never arrives.

289
00:14:15,564 --> 00:14:17,274
Under the Australian Consumer Law,

290
00:14:17,324 --> 00:14:20,374
if a business takes your money for
something and then can't supply it,

291
00:14:20,424 --> 00:14:22,594
you're generally entitled
to get that money back.

292
00:14:22,644 --> 00:14:26,374
And any contract term that lets a
business keep your deposit unfairly can be

293
00:14:26,424 --> 00:14:28,734
challenged as an unfair contract term.

294
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:32,174
So if a car company ever cancels a model
you've paid for and doesn't offer a

295
00:14:32,224 --> 00:14:34,094
refund, don't just accept it.

296
00:14:34,144 --> 00:14:35,534
Put your request in writing,

297
00:14:35,584 --> 00:14:39,674
and if you get nowhere, contact your
state's fair trading office or the ACCC.

298
00:14:39,724 --> 00:14:43,514
And if you're one of the Australians
who still had a Cybertruck reservation,

299
00:14:43,564 --> 00:14:45,074
here's the practical part.

300
00:14:45,124 --> 00:14:46,834
Keep a copy of Tesla's email.

301
00:14:46,884 --> 00:14:50,214
Log in to your Tesla account and
check that the reservation shows as

302
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:50,774
cancelled.

303
00:14:50,824 --> 00:14:55,054
Note the date, because Tesla says the
refund should arrive within thirty days.

304
00:14:55,104 --> 00:14:58,784
If it doesn't, follow up in writing,
keep the reply, and only then escalate.

305
00:14:58,834 --> 00:15:01,954
A hundred and fifty dollars
might not sound like much,

306
00:15:02,004 --> 00:15:05,104
but it's your money, and you've
already waited seven years for it.

307
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:09,548
So, the Tesla Cybertruck is
officially dead in Australia.

308
00:15:09,598 --> 00:15:12,368
Seven years, a $150 deposit,

309
00:15:12,418 --> 00:15:17,128
a national roadshow and a lot of hope
and it ends with an email and a refund.

310
00:15:17,178 --> 00:15:19,608
So what are the lessons
from the Cybertruck saga?

311
00:15:19,658 --> 00:15:22,348
Lesson one: a reveal is not a product.

312
00:15:22,398 --> 00:15:23,808
A concept on a stage,

313
00:15:23,858 --> 00:15:27,588
a price on a slide and a reservation
button don't mean a car is coming to

314
00:15:27,638 --> 00:15:31,148
Australia especially if it's
only built in left-hand drive.

315
00:15:31,198 --> 00:15:33,148
Lesson two: right-hand drive matters.

316
00:15:33,198 --> 00:15:36,808
Australia is a relatively
small right-hand-drive market.

317
00:15:36,858 --> 00:15:39,668
When a car maker has to choose
where to spend engineering money,

318
00:15:39,718 --> 00:15:41,508
we're not always first in line.

319
00:15:41,558 --> 00:15:44,928
Lesson three: the best car for
you is one you can actually buy,

320
00:15:44,978 --> 00:15:46,748
service and resell here.

321
00:15:46,798 --> 00:15:50,128
Hype doesn't fix a recall,
find a part or hold its value.

322
00:15:50,178 --> 00:15:53,428
The truth is, the Cybertruck was
always going to struggle here.

323
00:15:53,478 --> 00:15:55,868
Left-hand drive only, a huge price,

324
00:15:55,918 --> 00:15:58,748
a tiny segment and
falling sales in America.

325
00:15:58,798 --> 00:16:00,188
Tesla made the business call.

326
00:16:00,238 --> 00:16:03,468
And the electric ute race in Australia
will be fought by more practical

327
00:16:03,518 --> 00:16:04,568
machines.

328
00:16:04,618 --> 00:16:05,548
What do you think?

329
00:16:05,598 --> 00:16:09,048
Would you have bought a
Cybertruck at around $130,000?

330
00:16:09,098 --> 00:16:10,428
Tell me in the comments.

331
00:16:10,478 --> 00:16:13,028
If you enjoyed this,
hit like and subscribe.

332
00:16:13,078 --> 00:16:14,188
And in the next video,

333
00:16:14,238 --> 00:16:17,988
we're looking at what really happens
after you crash a BYD in Australia the

334
00:16:18,038 --> 00:16:22,348
wait, the repair bill and the insurance
renewal that nobody warns you about.

335
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,238
See you there.
